module main

-- §14.4 soundness (NEGATIVE): a generic equality `(=) xs ys` over an
-- ABSTRACT element type `a` is NOT an h-prop, so `unsafeAssertProof`
-- cannot construct it: the IsProp-under-Pi closure solver reaches
-- `IsProp ((=) xs ys)` over carrier `List a`, finds no `IsSet (List a)`
-- evidence, refuses to fabricate set-ness, and the assertion is REJECTED
-- (E_UNSOLVED_IMPLICIT).
--
-- Under §14.1.1's `trait IsSet a => Eq` supertrait, the standard
-- `Eq a => Eq (List a)` instance forces the CONDITIONAL
-- `IsSet a => IsSet (List a)` to exist (a well-formed instance must
-- discharge its supertrait), so at set-carriers like `List Bool` the
-- IsSet goal IS solvable — see tests/pending-import/spec-coverage/
-- nat-fin-refinement/positive/isset-supertrait-closure. What must stay
-- absent is the UNCONDITIONAL `IsSet (List a)`: this test is red only
-- because `a` here is abstract with no `Eq a`/`IsSet a` premise in scope,
-- so no conditional instance or supertrait projection can fire.
--
-- Were an unconditional `IsSet (List a)` admitted, `bogus` below would
-- type-check and a `subst` over a discriminator type family would
-- transport `Unit` into `Void`, inhabiting `Void` — the soundness
-- catastrophe pinned closed for carriers with no `Eq` in their supertrait
-- closure by tests/pending-import/spec-coverage/nat-fin-refinement/
-- negative/unsafe-assert-no-isset-function-carrier. List's monoid laws
-- are instead PROVEN by honest structural induction (see
-- `listAppendAssoc`).

bogus : forall (a : Type) (xs : List a) (ys : List a). (=) xs ys
let bogus = unsafeAssertProof "spec-forbidden: List a is not a set at abstract a"

--! mode check
--! allow_unsafe_assert_proof
--! assertDiagnostic error E_UNSOLVED_IMPLICIT
